From: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] warp: add ring lifecycle state machine, IRQ synchronization,
 and SER reset unwind

Introduce checked ring init/exit serialization, synchronize IRQs before teardown, propagate reset_rx_traffic errors, and retain bus/DMA resources on reset failure instead of risking double free.
Signed-off-by: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 regs/reg_v1/warp_hw_v1.c |   4 +
 regs/reg_v2/warp_hw_v2.c |  36 ++--
 regs/reg_v3/warp_hw.c    |  23 ++-
 regs/reg_v3_1/warp_hw.c  |  23 ++-
 regs/reg_v3_2/warp_hw.c  |  23 ++-
 warp.h                   |  35 ++++
 warp_main.c              | 374 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 warp_rx_bm.c             |  99 ++++++++---
 warp_rx_page_bm.c        |  47 ++++-
 warp_tx_bm_v2.c          |  23 +++
 warp_utility.c           |   5 +-
 warp_utility.h           |   2 +
 wdma.c                   |  22 ++-
 wed.c                    | 126 ++++++++++---
 14 files changed, 712 insertions(+), 130 deletions(-)

